title: ActFourNotes
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: The hearing
style: note
---
Act IV, the day of the fair. The village again, with the fair, a child scene the story loads while $fair_up is true (the cartographer does not move: the stalls and the hearing table are simply there). The steward's figure stands at the fair and the village's is hidden: the same actor never shows twice. Speak for the mill only if the cartographer took a side on the road; Lio's first map only if Lio was not blamed. The hearing gives one of six endings.
===

title: Events
act: Fair
location: Village
scenario: The hearing
quest: border
when: once
when: $act == Act.Fair
when: here() == "Village"
---
Ashcombe is full. Stalls on the green, flags over the bridge, and half the abbey in grey robes.
At the far end of the green, a long table: the hearing, at noon. The Countess, the Prior, and an empty chair for the cartographer.
<<if $jory_found>>
    Jory is at the front of the crowd, on a crutch, waving at you.
<<endif>>
<<set $quest_border to QuestState.Active>>
<<quest_changed border>>
===

title: Bram
act: Fair
location: Village
scenario: The road
quest: mill
when: $act == Act.Fair
when: $quest_mill == QuestState.NotStarted and ($road == Road.Corvin or $road == Road.Miller)
---
<<if $road == Road.Miller>>
    Bram: You said it yourself. The road goes around the mill. Will you say it again, at the table, in front of the steward?
<<else>>
    Bram: You sided with the steward, I know. But you've seen the mill now. Will you speak for us at the table?
<<endif>>
-> I will speak for the mill.
    Bram: That's all I ask.
    <<set $quest_mill to QuestState.Active>>
-> The map speaks for itself.
    Bram: Maps don't speak. People do. #mood:sad
    <<set $quest_mill to QuestState.Failed>>
<<quest_changed mill>>
===

title: Lio
act: Fair
location: Mill
scenario: Accounts
quest: lio_map
when: $act == Act.Fair
when: $culprit != Culprit.Lio and $quest_lio_map == QuestState.NotStarted
---
<<if $culprit == Culprit.Pell>>
    Lio: They let Pell go. I told Maren it was me, after. She said she knew.
<<endif>>
Lio: I made it. My first real map. The stones, the bridge, the river, and the old line, the way grandmother told it.
Lio: Take it to the table. It's better than nothing, and maybe better than something.
<<give lio_map>>
<<set $quest_lio_map to QuestState.Succeeded>>
<<quest_changed lio_map>>
===

title: Lio
act: All
location: Mill
scenario: Accounts
when: $act == Act.Castle or ($act == Act.Fair and ($culprit == Culprit.Lio or $quest_lio_map != QuestState.NotStarted))
---
<<if $act == Act.Castle>>
    Lio: You were at the castle! Is it true they eat off silver?
<<elseif $culprit == Culprit.Lio>>
    Lio: Go and draw your border. You know where I'd draw it. #mood:angry
<<else>>
    Lio: Is my map on the table? Is it?
<<endif>>
===

title: Corvin
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: The hearing
when: $act == Act.Fair
---
<<if $offer == Offer.Accepted>>
    Corvin: You have my border. Old ink, brown, not black. Don't disappoint me.
<<elseif $corvin_fate == CorvinFate.Helped>>
    Corvin: The cartographer who pulled me out of the dark. I have a map of my own today. I hope you understand.
<<elseif $corvin_fate == CorvinFate.Robbed>>
    Corvin: Somebody took my notebook in the mine. You wouldn't know who, I suppose. #mood:angry
<<else>>
    Corvin: Today we see whose map the valley believes.
<<endif>>
===

title: Anselm
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: The hearing
when: $act == Act.Fair
---
=> Anselm: Prior Anselm, of the abbey. The river has been our border for three hundred years. Rivers do not lie.
=> Anselm: Your map will be the fourth one I have seen this year. The other three agreed with whoever paid for them.
=> Anselm: They say you went under the hill. What did you find there? Nothing, I hope. <<if $carvings_copied>>
===

title: Hearing
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: The hearing
quest: border
when: $act == Act.Fair and $quest_border == QuestState.Active
---
// The sixth fork and the ending: the border drawn at the hearing, with what the other forks left on the table.
You take the empty chair at the long table. The green goes quiet.
Ysolde: The cartographer has surveyed the valley at my charge. Let us see the map.
Anselm: And let us see if it agrees with the river.
<<if $map_incomplete>>
    You unroll your map. [plural value={survey_count()} one="One landmark" other="% landmarks" /], and blank parchment where the rest should be.
    Anselm: A map with holes is no map. The abbey will not sign this.
    Ysolde: Nor will I. #mood:angry
    <<set $quest_border to QuestState.Failed>>
    <<quest_changed border>>
    <<set $outcome to "failed">>
    <<jump Epilogue>>
<<endif>>
<<if $corvin_presents>>
    Corvin: The castle has a map of its own. An old one, from the archive. Please. Look at the line.
    He unrolls a brown, crackling sheet. The border on it runs well inside the abbey's meadows.
<<endif>>
<<if $quest_mill == QuestState.Active>>
    Bram stands at the edge of the crowd, looking at you.
    -> Speak for the mill. The road should go around it.
        <<set $spoke_for_mill to true>>
        Ysolde: The mill has ground the valley's bread for a hundred years. Noted.
        <<set $quest_mill to QuestState.Succeeded>>
    -> Say nothing about the mill.
        Bram turns away.
        <<set $quest_mill to QuestState.Failed>>
    <<quest_changed mill>>
<<endif>>
-> Draw the carved border, from the stones under the hill. <<if $carvings_copied>>
    <<set $border to Border.Carved>>
    You draw the carved line across the map, from the bridge stone north under the hill to the abbey's well.
    <<if $corvin_presents and $has_proof>>
        <<jump Exposed>>
    <<elseif $corvin_presents and $corvin_fate == CorvinFate.Helped>>
        Corvin looks at your line for a long time.
        Corvin: You pulled me out of the dark. I won't call you a liar in front of the valley. The castle withdraws its map.
    <<elseif $corvin_presents>>
        Anselm: Two old maps, and two borders. The steward's has the castle's seal. Yours has a cartographer's word.
        Anselm: The abbey would rather have the steward's meadows than a ghost's carvings.
        <<set $outcome to "forged">>
        <<jump Epilogue>>
    <<endif>>
    <<if $can_draw_true_border>>
        Anselm: The charter's page says the same. The abbey cannot argue with its own founder's hand.
    <<else>>
        Anselm: Carvings in a mine. Well. They are older than the river's last flood, I give you that.
    <<endif>>
    <<if $road_around>>
        <<set $outcome to "true_around">>
    <<else>>
        <<set $outcome to "true_through">>
    <<endif>>
-> Draw the steward's border. <<if has_item("false_map")>>
    <<set $border to Border.Forged>>
    You draw Corvin's line, the one he paid for. Old ink, brown, not black.
    Corvin smiles for the first time in the whole story.
    <<set $outcome to "forged">>
-> Show the proof that the steward's map is forged. <<if $corvin_presents and $has_proof>>
    <<jump Exposed>>
-> Draw the path the villagers walk, from stone to stone.
    <<set $border to Border.Walked>>
    You draw the line the village walks every spring, beating the bounds from stone to stone. Nobody's, everybody's.
    <<if has_item("lio_map")>>
        You lay Lio's map beside it. The two lines agree almost everywhere.
    <<endif>>
    Anselm: A compromise. I hate compromises. Very well.
    <<set $outcome to "walked">>
<<set $quest_border to QuestState.Succeeded>>
<<quest_changed border>>
<<jump Epilogue>>
===

title: Exposed
act: Fair
location: Fair
scenario: The hearing
quest: border
---
<<if has_item("letter")>>
    You lay the steward's letter on the table. "Draw it so, and it is worth forty crowns to you." In his own hand.
<<else>>
    You lay the steward's notebook on the table, open. The same border, drawn again and again, older-looking each time.
<<endif>>
The green goes very quiet.
Ysolde: Corvin. My study. Now. #mood:angry
Corvin does not go to her study. He goes to the stables.
<<set $border to Border.Carved>>
<<set $outcome to "exposed">>
<<set $quest_border to QuestState.Succeeded>>
<<quest_changed border>>
<<jump Epilogue>>
===

title: Hearing
act: All
location: Fair
scenario: The hearing
when: $quest_border != QuestState.Active
---
The hearing table is empty now. Somebody has left a cup of cider on it.
===
